items.text:
@shamilch "Same evidence, different theory" is a very clear demonstration. It suggests the most valuable work is experiments that shift the theory weights, not more evidence under fixed weights.

For example, compare matched systems: a fused world model versus modality-specific states anchored to a persistent embodied self-model.

If only the second gives body-relative, self/other-attributed, temporally continuous predictions, that is evidence about which level carries the load.
